    "q-251794": {
      "dom_id": "step-q251794",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Consider two sets of $14$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{14},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{14}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{14}{x}_{i}=157, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{14}{y}_{i}=182, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{14}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=2\\,227.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, ${S}_{xy}=$\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the statistic ${S}_{xy}$ be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}-\\frac{1}{n}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given statistics in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & =2\\,227-\\frac{1}{14}(157)(182) \\\\  & =2\\,227-2\\,041 \\\\  & =186.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
